{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a plain sink with one requirement, "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which is given"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a batch of records, oldest first. Delivering is a chain of operators over a tracker’s records:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch()"},{"type":"text","text":" gathers them into batches of 20, and every 30 seconds while any are pending, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:bufferDropReporter:)"},{"type":"text","text":" hands each batch to every destination as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lazy unit of work that runs once you call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"execute()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each destination receives its batches in order, one at a time, from a buffer of its own, so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"slow one delays only itself. A full buffer drops its oldest batch and reports it as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/BufferDropReport","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". When the tracker has a store, the delivery reads the dropped batch’s records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"back for that destination once it catches up, and tells the store when each batch has reached"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every destination."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What a destination receives is narrowed by modifiers: "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/accepting(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consent categories it serves, "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/redactingSensitiveValues()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/droppingCallSite()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", and added to by "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/enriched(by:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", which runs an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Enricher","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" on the records that destination alone receives. "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/ConsoleDestination","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"prints each event, and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps the newest records it receives for the app to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"read, in a debug view or a test."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Logs, traces and servers have destinations in modules of their own, so an app links only the ones"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it uses: "},{"code":"LoggerDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"code":"LoggingDestinations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"SpanEventDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"TracingDestinations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"code":"HTTPDestinations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct Uploader: Destination {","    func receive(_ batch: [EventRecord]) async {","        \/\/ Send the batch, and return once it is somewhere it won't be lost.","    }","}","","let inspector = try InMemoryDestination(capacity: 500)","let tracker = Tracker()","let delivery = tracker.records","    .batch(strategy: .count(20))","    .deliver(","        to: Uploader().accepting(.analytics).redactingSensitiveValues().droppingCallSite(),","        inspector","    )","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))","await tracker.finish()","try await delivery.execute()","let received = inspector.events(of: SignedUp.self)  \/\/ [SignedUp(plan: \"pro\")]"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The umbrella guide on this area is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/destinations"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Destinations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/ConsoleDestination","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InMemoryDestination","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/InvalidCapacity"],"anchor":"Destinations"},{"title":"Delivering","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/_Concurrency\/AsyncSequence\/batch(clock:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/_Concurrency\/AsyncSequence\/deliver(to:bufferDropRe